course: dictionary
lesson: 15601
title: Talks: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word talks can mean different things, and context shows you which one. Read the words around it first. «She talks to her dog every morning.» Here talks is the form of talk we use with she, so it means she speaks to her dog.
explain: «Peace talks between the two countries start on Monday.» Here talks is a noun. Talks are formal meetings where people try to reach an agreement. The word peace tells you what the meetings are about.
explain: «The firefighter gives talks at our school.» Now talks means speeches or presentations given to an audience. The words gives and school are your clues. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Talks is the form of talk used with he, she or it: she talks, he talks, it talks.
fact: Talks as a noun is the plural of talk, so one talk can become two talks.
fact: «Peace talks» and «trade talks» are formal meetings between leaders or countries to reach an agreement.
fact: Talks can also be speeches or presentations given to an audience, such as a visitor talking to a class.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Our teacher talks about dinosaurs.» What does talks mean here? | Writes a letter | Walks slowly | *Speaks about a subject | Sings loudly
exercise: «Peace talks between the two countries start on Monday.» What are peace talks? | *Formal meetings to reach an agreement | Songs about peace | Lessons about the weather | Games played in a park
exercise: «The firefighter gives talks at our school.» What are talks in this sentence? | Fires put out in the school hall | *Speeches given to an audience | Tests for every class | School holidays
test: Dad ___ about his new car all day. Which word fits? | *talks | talking | talk | talked
test: What are trade talks? | *Meetings between countries to agree on trade | Lessons about money in maths | Shopping trips for the whole family | Races between traders
exam: In «The parrot talks», why does talks end in -s? | *Because the parrot is one thing and talks is the present form for it | Because the sentence is in the past | Because the parrot is many birds | Because talks is a noun here
